## Scope

The project is maintained by Artificial Intelligence Advancement Initiative Inc.
This document explains technical decision-making and maintenance responsibilities.
Contribution and licensing terms are in [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md), and
participation standards are in [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).

## Proposing changes

Use [issues]({{REPOSITORY_URL}}/issues) and
[pull requests]({{REPOSITORY_URL}}/pulls) to propose changes.
For substantial proposals, describe the problem, alternatives, compatibility
impact, maintenance cost, and proposed validation. Keep security reports private
as described in [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md).

## Decisions

{{TECHNICAL_DECISION_PROCESS}}

When a proposal cannot reach agreement, the final decision authority is:

{{FINAL_DECISION_AUTHORITY}}

Record significant decisions and their reasoning in the relevant discussion or
project documentation. Apply the repository's configured review and check
requirements. Technical disagreement does not exempt anyone from the code of
conduct.

## Maintenance responsibilities

See [MAINTAINERS.md](MAINTAINERS.md) for the actual roster and responsibilities.
The process for adding, changing, or ending maintenance roles is:

{{MAINTAINER_APPOINTMENT_PROCESS}}

Update the roster, code ownership, and GitHub access when roles change. Changes
to this governance document should follow the decision process above.
